<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Todar Mal</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1589">1589</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Raja Todar Mal</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Todar Mal was the finance minister of the Mughal emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akbar">Akbar</a> and one of the leading nobles of his court. He reorganised land revenue through the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zabt-system">zabt</a> system, which assessed taxes in cash from measured land and average yields and prices, and his methods long shaped revenue administration in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. He also commanded armies in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bengal">Bengal</a>, and died in 1589.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/todar-mal.jpg" alt="Todar Mal" width="320" height="509" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Indian, Moghul · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Raja_Todar_Mall,_Finance_Minister_of_Akbar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
